========================================================================================================
K3  THE BARE INTEGRAL  I_bare(Y) = Int_0^Y y(nu-1) dy  (the integral the record writes as (1/2)Int(nu-1)d(y^2))
========================================================================================================
    exact antiderivative, Langmuir :  I_L(Y) = Y**(3/2)*sqrt(Y + 4)/4 + sqrt(Y)*sqrt(Y + 4)/2 - Y**2/4 - 2*acosh(sqrt(Y + 4)/2)
    exact antiderivative, quadrature:  I_Q(Y) = Y**(3/2)*sqrt(Y + 1)/2 + sqrt(Y)*sqrt(Y + 1)/4 - Y**2/2 - acosh(sqrt(Y + 1))/4
    compact form,  Langmuir :  I_L(Y) = [(Y+2)sqrt(Y^2+4Y) - Y^2]/4 - ln[(Y+2+sqrt(Y^2+4Y))/2]
    compact form, quadrature:  I_Q(Y) = [(2Y+1)sqrt(Y^2+Y) - 2Y^2]/4 - ln[sqrt(Y+1)+sqrt(Y)]/4
    compact vs sympy antiderivative at Y = 1e5: max rel 8.4e-12  (double-precision evaluation; the identity is acosh z = ln(z+sqrt(z^2-1)))
    exact, RAR    :  I_R(inf) = 2*Gamma(4)*zeta(4) = 2*pi**4/15 = 2*pi^4/15 = 12.987878804533658
                     (substituting y = u^2 turns Int y/(e^sqrt y - 1) dy into 2 Int u^3/(e^u - 1) du)
    exact, nu_mono:  diverges (h_M -> delta*h_p*ln y, so Int h_M dy ~ delta*h_p*Y ln Y)
    closed form vs adaptive quadrature at Y = 1e3, 1e6: max rel 3.17e-26
    incremental slope dI/dY: L 0.999999953 (->1), Q 0.499999994 (->1/2)
    I_L(1e8) - 1e8 + ln(1e8) = 0.499999980   (constant 1/2)
    I_Q(1e8) - 5e7 + ln(1e8)/8 = -0.110786796 (constant -0.1107868)
  K3   PASS closed forms certified: max rel 3.2e-26 (quad), 8.4e-12 (compact); dI/dY = 0.999999953 (L), 0.499999994 (Q); I_R(inf) = 12.987878804534
        threshold: rel<1e-9 vs quadrature, <1e-10 compact; slopes 1 and 1/2 to 1e-6; I_R = 2pi^4/15 exactly

